Yes, 14 Mill Wynd is in the Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area. It is not a listed building and is not covered by a tree preservation order.

Under the council's windows guidance, replacing windows in a conservation area needs planning permission unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material, style or glazing pattern, you should apply before starting work. If you are only replacing like-for-like, you may not need an application, but I can't give a formal opinion on that. It's worth contacting the planning desk to confirm before you order anything.

If you have already submitted an application for this work, please give me the reference (in the format 00/00000/XXX) and I can look up its status.
